# Copy to .env for local overrides. Every variable is optional in development
# and test; safe defaults point at the docker-compose PostgreSQL instance.
# In production, DATABASE_URL is required and has no default.

# development | test | production
NODE_ENV=development
# fatal | error | warn | info | debug | trace | silent
LOG_LEVEL=debug
HTTP_HOST=127.0.0.1
HTTP_PORT=3000
DATABASE_URL=postgres://ltw:ltw_dev_password@127.0.0.1:54329/ltw
# dev-personas (default outside production; refused in production) | disabled
AUTH_MODE=dev-personas
# Persona token file for dev-personas mode (default: fixtures/ravenford/personas.json)
# DEV_PERSONAS_FILE=/absolute/path/personas.json
# AI gateway (docs/adr/0017-ai-gateway.md). Without a key only the deterministic
# local provider runs. The key is never logged or traced.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# LTW_AI_MODEL=claude-opus-5-5
# LTW_AI_TIMEOUT_MS=30000
# How long a context request with ranking=ai waits for the relevance ranker
# before answering with the deterministic ranking (docs/adr/0021-ai-relevance.md).
# LTW_AI_RELEVANCE_BUDGET_MS=2000

# Live AI, Stage 300 (docs/adr/0032-live-ai.md). Keys go in .env.local, never in the repository.
# DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=
# LTW_DEEPSEEK_MODEL=deepseek-flash
# Each capability's providers in order, `provider:model`: `local`, or one remote then `local`
# (relevance: one remote only). Three entries, two remotes, or a remote without its key are startup
# errors. A key alone implies no route. In the current build (Stage 300 remediation checkpoint B1)
# remote routes are reported as disabled and never constructed: every capability runs locally.
# LTW_AI_ROUTES=reasoning=anthropic:claude-opus-5-5,local;npc-dialogue=anthropic:claude-sonnet-5-5,local;narrative=anthropic:claude-opus-5-5,local;fast-context=deepseek:deepseek-flash
# Spending ceilings are not environment settings: they are operator records (`pnpm ai:operator`,
# docs/adr/0032-live-ai.md). LTW_AI_DAILY_BUDGET_USD was removed and is ignored with a warning.
